:0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797153189","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99543#issuecomment-2797153189","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99543","id":2797153189,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6muSul","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-11T14:56:39Z","updated_at":"2025-04-11T14:56:39Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2797153189/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2922562673","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99543#issuecomment-2922562673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99543","id":2922562673,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uMsRx","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T14:31:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T14:31:57Z","body":"So recently I came across this article:\r\nhttps://web.archive.org/web/20150124024222/http://blogs.unity3d.com/2015/01/07/a-primer-on-repeatable-random-numbers/\r\n\r\nEspecially the paragraph about different seed values, which claims that numbers across seeds are not really random in relation to each other.\r\n![](https://web.archive.org/web/20150124024222im_/http://blogs.unity3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/TwoRNGs.png)\r\nThis is what this PR does - it creates a new seeded RNG for each UID.\r\n\r\nI don't know if the above is true for _our_ RNG though, maybe it doesn't have this problem. But if it does, there is a higher chance of conflicting UIDs now. Would be nice if someone can confirm. We generate 2 numbers and do some bit magic, but still.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2922562673/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2923488269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99543#issuecomment-2923488269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99543","id":2923488269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uQOQN","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T21:05:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T21:05:30Z","body":"Looking more at the code I wouldn't expect there to be problems in practice. A hash function is a better choice in theory at a minimum because we'd like collision resistance, and and ideal PRNGs should still produce collisions. However, in the code above, the initial seed for the PRNG is generated via hash functions and generates enough data to fill the entire internal state of the PRNG, which is functionally equivalent to choosing a random possible state of the PRNG. \r\n\r\nThere's technically one way that this could still be worse, depending on the distribution of likelihoods of the internal states of the PRNG during a sequence of generations, but I haven't heard of that being a problem before and isn't what that article is concerned about.\r\n\r\nIf the input seed wasn't coming from a hash, I'd have concerns, but I would expect this to be basically as good as using the PRNG seeded more traditionally. The main problem that article points out is that correlations between seeds can leak into correlations between outputs, but the use of hashes on the seed should have already removed correlations in the seeds. The article actually even mentions this option:\r\n> if multiple seeds are used they should be passed through a random hash function (such as xxHash) first.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2923488269/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2923503846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99543#issuecomment-2923503846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99543","id":2923503846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uQSDm","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T21:10:12Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T21:30:10Z","body":"My one actual nit is this bit `project_name.hash64() * p_path.hash64() * FileAccess::get_md5(p_path).hash64()`.\r\n\r\nTypically XOR or ADD is used instead of MUL because it introduces issues if any of them happen to be zero. That should basically not happen for the lifetime of the universe, but I'm unfamiliar with whether there are additional issues with multiplication.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2923503846/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]